        "original_id": "3970f289-e4c0-57b8-9b8f-5de6f0a44a98",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Plants: Crowea, Dracula\n- Concepts: species counts, subspecies, cultivars, ornamentals, horticultural abbreviations, native ranges\n- Places: Mexico, Central America, Colombia, Ecuador, Peru\n\nFacts:\n- Crowea has three species and many subspecies and cultivars.\n- Crowea plants are popular ornamentals because they have abundant, attractive flowers that often appear during autumn and winter.\n- The orchid genus Dracula is abbreviated as Drac in horticultural trade.\n- The orchid genus Dracula consists of 118 species.\n- Dracula is native to Mexico, Central America, Colombia, Ecuador, and Peru.",
